    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0662" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.24/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Weeks</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose a translation
                    of a communication recently received from the Government of Nicaragua,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d503-f1"/> inquiring whether this Government can supply
                    certain arms and munitions from stocks left on hand by the war. This
                    communication is transmitted to you for your information, and I should
                    appreciate an expression of opinion from you as to whether the supplies desired
                    by Nicaragua can be furnished by this Government. In view of the political
                    situation referred to by the Nicaraguan Minister, the need for these arms and
                    munitions is rather urgent.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Under
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
